    {
      "clause": "Every open coordinate and its actual base case",
      "assessment": "For a one-leaf interval, any nonunary composition would have a child of strictly positive leaf count strictly below one, a contradiction. Thus the lower composition sum is empty and the source b coordinate and E coordinate are both one. For a longer interval, the accepted open-tree recursion gives b as minus the complete nonunary product sum. Casting that equality and replacing the actual ordinary weights by their exact geometric half factors makes the identical lower sum cancel in Phi. This proves equality of the entire interval array, without replacing b by a newly chosen solution."
